VERDICT -- gainfair
===================
BOTH ARMS LOSE.  STOPPED AFTER REPLICATE 1; NEITHER SIGN WAS CLOSE.

        B med       J = +GAINFAIR   J vs B  |  K = +GAINFAIR+PROBE   K vs B
  P1      571,668       571,668      0.0%   |        543,874        - 4.9%
  P3    4,468,072     4,468,072      0.0%   |      4,791,019        + 7.2%
  P7      749,573       747,511      -0.3%  |        877,593        +17.1%
  P16   3,022,891     3,186,941      +5.4%  |      2,956,901        - 2.2%
  P27     692,860       865,776     +25.0%  |        854,533        +23.3%
  P33     933,974       952,955      +2.0%  |      1,058,311        +13.3%
  sum  10,439,038    10,792,923     +3.39%  |     11,082,231        +6.16%

THE DIAGNOSIS WAS RIGHT AND THE REPAIR IS WORTHLESS.  The floor-escape credit really does decide
selection -- with it dropped, OPSTAT shows pref going from 3 tries on 11.1% of the budget to 7 tries
on 28.0%, and beam from 29.4% to 11.4%.  The budget genuinely moves.  The ANSWER does not: prob_1
and prob_3 return B's value to the digit and prob_7 to within 0.3%.

THE PAIRING HYPOTHESIS WAS ALSO RIGHT, AND ALSO NOT ENOUGH.  probe.log lost 32.8-37.5% on prob_16
and 48.1-59.3% on prob_7; with the gain fix underneath, prob_16 becomes a 2.2% WIN and prob_7's loss
shrinks to 17.1%.  So the probe cap was dangerous only because the race decided everything.
Defusing it still leaves K 6.16% behind B.

WHAT THIS CLOSES.  Six routes have now been tried against prob_1's unused clock and its 571,668
attractor: a longer round (B itself), two rounds, three rounds, deleting the zero-paying operator,
capping the opening probe, and repairing the selection signal that governs all of them.  Every
reallocation lands on the same value.  The scheduler is not what holds this instance; what would
move it is a better SEARCH, not a better division of the budget among the searches there are.

OGC_PROBE and OGC_GAINFAIR both stay in the file at default off, byte-identical.  They are the
instruments that established the above and each is one env away.

SHIPPING DECISION UNCHANGED: B, delivered as OGC2026_capfix.zip.

CORRECTION -- THE K ARM IS VOID
===============================
K was "0.05 + GAINFAIR + OGC_PROBE=2", and OGC_PROBE collided with a pre-existing variable meaning
the repair passes' opening slice as a fraction of the budget.  K therefore also opened every repair
operator at 50% of the clock.  Its numbers -- prob_16 -2.2%, prob_7 +17.1%, sum +6.16% -- measure
that, not the first-try cap, and the claim that the gain fix "defuses" the probe cap is withdrawn.

THE J ARM STANDS.  It sets only OGC_GAINFAIR=1 and touches no colliding name: +3.39% over the band,
with prob_1 and prob_3 returning B's value to the digit and prob_27 losing 25.0%.  The finding it
supports is unchanged and is the one that mattered: dropping the floor-escape credit really does
reallocate the budget (pref 11.1% -> 28.0% of the clock, beam 29.4% -> 11.4%) and the answers do
not move.
